// ========================================================================
// ICON SYSTEM — MASTER DOCUMENTATION
// ========================================================================
//
// This section defines the complete icon vocabulary for the media dashboard.
// All icons used anywhere in the system MUST be defined here.
//
// PURPOSE:
//   - Centralize icon definitions
//   - Ensure deterministic behavior across UI, scripts, and controller logic
//   - Prevent icon overloading or duplication
//   - Provide full documentation for each icon
//
// HOW ICONS ARE USED:
//   - UI components reference icons via config.icons.<key>.icon
//   - Scripts reference icons via config.icons.<key>
//   - No icon may be hardcoded anywhere else in the codebase
//
// FUNCTION TYPE BEHAVIOR:
//   - "single-click": instant action (e.g., toggle watched)
//   - "popup": opens a modal or multi-choice dialog
//   - "long-press": opens extended menu (D-pad compatible)
//   - "link": opens external or internal URL
//   - "function": triggers internal logic (e.g., sync)
//
// D-PAD BEHAVIOR:
//   - Single-click actions activate on press
//   - Popup actions open a modal or menu on press
//   - Long-press actions open a secondary menu on press
//   - Link actions open the associated URL on press
//
// TRAKT SYNC:
//   - Sync actions map to Trakt endpoints or local proxy actions
//   - All sync actions must be deterministic and idempotent
//
// CUSTOM MEDIA SOURCES:
//   - Vidrsc and VidEasy are complementary icons
//   - Both use streaming base URLs + TMDB slug
//
// ADDING NEW ICONS:
//   - Add a full documentation block above the icon entry
//   - Ensure the icon is unique and not overloaded
//   - Define purpose, functionType, and target
//   - Update scripts and UI to reference the new icon key
//
// ========================================================================
